  <data name="ActivityScenarioTitle1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Improper Disposal</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioPrompt1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A neighborhood store is dumping used motor oil behind the building. What should happen first?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioOption1A" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Report it and suggest safe disposal options</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioOption1B" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ignore it because it is not on your land</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioOption1C" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pour water to dilute the oil</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioFeedback1A" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Correct. Reporting and safer disposal stop pollution at the source.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioFeedback1B" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Not quite. Ignoring leaks allows contamination to spread.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioFeedback1C" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Not quite. Diluting can spread pollutants further.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioTitle2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pesticide Runoff</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioPrompt2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A farm sprays pesticides before a heavy rain. What is the best next step?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioOption2A" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Delay spraying and check the weather forecast</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioOption2B" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Spray more to make it last longer</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioOption2C" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Wash pesticides into nearby drains</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioFeedback2A" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Correct. Timing and weather checks reduce runoff risk.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioFeedback2B" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Not quite. Overuse increases pollution and waste.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioFeedback2C" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Not quite. Washing chemicals into drains spreads pollution.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioTitle3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Construction Debris</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioPrompt3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A construction site leaves debris on bare soil. What is the safest practice?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioOption3A" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cover soil and remove waste to approved sites</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioOption3B" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Leave debris to mix with the soil</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioOption3C" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Burn debris on-site</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioFeedback3A" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Correct. Covering soil and proper disposal prevent contamination.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioFeedback3B" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Not quite. Debris can introduce contaminants into soil.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActivityScenarioFeedback3C" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Not quite. Burning can release toxins and ash into soil.</value>
  </data>
